    <documentation><![CDATA[
GoFanco Matrix44-HDBT (DriverWorks)

By Heatvent (with Claude). MIT License. Unofficial - not made or supported by gofanco or Snap One/Control4.

Full control driver for the gofanco Matrix44-HDBT (G4-0064B, HDMI 2.0 4x4 HDBaseT matrix kit) over RS-232 (9600 8N1) or over the network (the matrix's LAN port, TCP port 23). Uses the command set from the G4-0064B user guide (OUTxx:yy., PowerON., STA_VIDEO. ...). Pick the link with the Connection Type property.

TESTED ON
Matrix44-HDBT firmware V1.0.1 / CPLD V1.0.0, RS-232 from a Control4 EA-series controller, OS 3.4.3. The network port speaks the same commands as RS-232 (raw TCP, port 23, no line ending) and accepts more than one client at a time, so Control4 and another system (for example Home Assistant) can both be connected; each sees the other's changes. Other gofanco matrix models use a different command set ("1V3.", "%9964.") and will not work with this driver.

PORTS ON THIS MATRIX
Outputs 1-3 are HDBaseT (CAT) outputs with receivers. Output 4 is the HDMI output. "Output 5" in some commands is the HDMI loop-out of output 3.

WHAT IT DOES
- Routes video for Control4 rooms (AV switch proxy, 4 inputs, 4 outputs).
- Reads routing back (STA_VIDEO.) at startup and on a poll timer and shows it in "Output 1-4 Source". Front-panel / IR remote changes are picked up too.
- Actions for every command in the guide's RS-232 table: system info, status queries, board temperature, IP address and setting a new IP, presets 1-9, front-panel lock, power, route-to-all, HDCP modes, HDMI 5V, PoC power to receivers, IR follow video, IR routing, receiver IR-to-MCU, de-embedded audio source, EDID (built-in, copy from display, read display EDID, restore default, status), CEC control of sources and displays, raw commands, guarded factory reset.
- Not given buttons on purpose: "Baudrate" (changing it breaks the link to the controller), "EDIDUpgrade" (needs a .bin file upload), and "/+" pass-through. Use Send Raw Command if you ever need them.

SETUP - SERIAL (default)
1. Connect the matrix's RS-232 port (3-pin Phoenix; use the included Phoenix-to-DB9 cable) to a controller serial port.
2. Leave Connection Type on "Serial (RS-232)". In Composer, bind "Serial RS-232" to that controller serial port.

SETUP - NETWORK
1. Plug the matrix's LAN port into your network and give it a fixed address (a DHCP reservation in your router is easiest). Its web page shows the address.
2. Set Connection Type to "Network (TCP/IP)", IP Address to the matrix's address, and leave Network Port at 23.
3. No Composer network binding is needed; the driver opens the connection itself and reconnects if it drops. "Connection Status" shows the state.

THEN (both)
3. Bind the HDMI inputs to your sources and the outputs to your displays/receivers.
4. Refresh Navigators. The driver reads the current routing once connected; "Connection Status" should show Online.
5. Power Handling defaults to "Room On/Off sends PowerON/PowerOFF": the matrix powers on when any room starts using it and off when the last room using it turns off (Control4 only sends OFF to a shared device once no room is using it, so several rooms can share a source). Set it to Ignore to keep the matrix on all the time.

REPLACING A DRIVER BUILDER (.c4i) DRIVER
This driver uses the standard AV switch connection IDs (inputs 1000-1003, outputs 2000-2003, serial 1, proxy 5001) and the same OUTxx:yy. routing command, so it can replace a Composer Driver Builder driver for this matrix: back up the project, add this driver, move each binding across, then delete the old driver.

PROPERTIES THAT ARE INPUTS FOR ACTIONS
Route Input / Route Output -> Apply Route, Route Input To All Outputs
Preset Number -> Save / Recall / Show Preset
Output Selection -> HDCP, HDMI 5V, PoC, EDID copy source, Read Display EDID, CEC display, IR routing (local IR out)
Input Selection -> EDID built-in / copy target / status, CEC source
Receiver Selection -> IR routing (receiver IR in), receiver IR controls MCU
Built-in EDID Number -> EDID: Set Built-in
Audio Out Source -> Set Audio Out Source
New IP Address -> Set Matrix IP Address (a value stored by the matrix; the LAN port's real address is set in its web page)
Connection Type / IP Address / Network Port -> how the driver talks to the matrix
CEC Source Device Type (default 04 = Blu-ray) / CEC Display Device Type (TV: 40, 20 or 80) -> CEC actions
Raw Command -> Send Raw Command (a trailing "." is added if missing)
Confirm Factory Reset -> Factory Reset (RST.) only runs when set to "Yes, reset the matrix"

PROGRAMMING COMMANDS
Route Input To Output, Route Input To All Outputs, Recall Preset, Power On, Power Off, Refresh Status, Send Raw Command.
]]></documentation>
